Lares (Artificer): The census and red-first grant-reader tests are ready. I submitted the tests through the broker’s commit door; the commit remains pending, so the state file retains the launch head.

The tests cover a fresh-epoch founder edge with an aside standing, and a signed epoch-free edge with clear standing. Each has a control. The standing test currently supplies a stubbed reading; a later integration test must exercise concurrent signed remove-wins acts and the pinned frontier. The controller must run the tests and confirm the expected failures.

The hand-back records the reader census, the lease-retirement decision, the b5b overlap, and the cure order: mesh relation, keyhive readers, node/browser readers, then the guarded roll and epoch-field burn.

